     `String parentTag = context.getDriver().getXmlParser().getTagName(parent);` -> wait, in `visitAttribute`, I can get parent via `attribute.getParentNode()` or `context.getElement().getParentNode()`. Actually, `visitAttribute` gives `Attribute attribute`. I can get `Element parent = (Element) attribute.getParentNode();` Wait, attribute's parent is the element it belongs to. I need the *parent element* of that element. So `Element view = (Element) attribute.getParentNode(); Element parentView = (Element) view.getParentNode();`

     Let's refine the parent extraction:
     ```java
     Node parentNode = attribute.getParentNode();
     if (!(parentNode instanceof Element)) return;
     Element view = (Element) parentNode;
     Node grandParentNode = view.getParentNode();
     if (!(grandParentNode instanceof Element)) return;
     Element parent = (Element) grandParentNode;
     String parentTag = parent.getTagName();
     // Strip namespace prefix if any
     int colon = parentTag.indexOf(':');
     if (colon != -1) parentTag = parentTag.substring(colon + 1);
